# Costco Financial Performance Dashboard (Power BI)

## Overview
An interactive 4-page Power BI dashboard analyzing Costco Wholesale Corporation's (NASDAQ: COST) financial performance from FY2021–FY2025, covering profitability, income statement structure, and balance sheet health.

**[View Dashboard Preview (PDF)](./Costco_Dashboard_Preview.pdf)** · **[Live Dashboard](#)** *(add your Power BI Service link here)*

## Business Question
How has Costco's financial performance evolved over the past five years, and what does that reveal about the sustainability of its growth?

## Data Source
Financial statement data compiled from Costco's audited 10-K filings, FY2021–FY2025, via [stockanalysis.com](https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/COST/financials/).

## Tools & Techniques
- **Power Query** — data cleaning, unpivoting wide-format financials into a long/tall fact table, custom columns for statement categorization
- **Data Modeling** — star schema with a fact table (`FactFinancials`) and date dimension (`DimDate`)
- **DAX** — 15+ measures including profitability margins, liquidity ratios, leverage ratios, and a signed waterfall measure for bridge chart logic
- **Report Design** — multi-page layout with consistent navigation, dynamic slicers, and visual-level filtering for period-specific KPIs

## Pages

**1. Cover** — Project overview and data source

**2. Executive Summary** — FY2025 snapshot (Revenue, Net Margin, ROE, Current Ratio) alongside a 5-year Revenue vs. Net Income trend

**3. Profitability Deep Dive** — Revenue-to-Net-Income bridge chart (FY2025) and 5-year margin trend analysis (Gross, Operating, Net)

**4. Balance Sheet & Liquidity** — Balance sheet composition (Liabilities vs. Equity) and liquidity/leverage trends (Current Ratio, Total Liabilities-to-Equity)

## Key Findings
- Revenue grew from $196B to $275B (FY2021–FY2025), while net margin expanded from 2.6% to 2.9%, reflecting disciplined cost management despite inflationary pressure
- COGS consumes roughly 87% of revenue, consistent with Costco's low-margin, high-volume retail model
- Total liabilities-to-equity declined from 2.3 to 1.7 over the period, while the current ratio held steady above 1.0 — indicating Costco strengthened its balance sheet while continuing to grow

